<div class="mb-12 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 p-6" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-5 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">Frequently asked questions</h2>
  <div class="mt-6 space-y-6">
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">What is an AI agent in plain English?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">Software that is given a goal and chooses its own steps and tools to reach it. Anthropic describes agents as systems where the model dynamically directs its own processes and tool usage, while a workflow follows steps defined in advance by people. A chatbot answers questions; an agent can also take actions such as booking an appointment.</p></div>
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">What should a small business automate first?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">One repeatable workflow with a clear definition of done, where a mistake is cheap and a person can check the result. Answering customer questions from your own documents and booking appointments are two examples we use. Do not start with payments, deletions or anything customer-facing without approval.</p></div>
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">How much does an AI agent cost?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">The sources behind this playbook publish no price lists, so we give none. What they do show is that more complex designs add cost and latency, and that Gartner expects over 40% of agentic AI projects to be cancelled by the end of 2027, partly because of escalating costs. Ask each supplier to price one real workflow and compare the quotes.</p></div>
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">Do I need to hire a technical person before I start?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">Not necessarily, but you do need a named owner inside the business who is accountable for the result, and a person who reviews the agent's work. The technical build can come from a supplier. What you cannot hand over is the decision about what the agent is allowed to do.</p></div>
  </div>
</div>

